\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My Jesus, I love Thee, I know Thou art mine,
\par For Thee all the pleasures of sin I resign;
\par My gracious Redeemer, my Saviour art Thou,
\par If ever I loved Thee, my Jesus, 'tis now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I love Thee because Thou hast first loved me,
\par And purchased my pardon on Calvary's tree;
\par I love Thee for wearing the thorns on Thy brow,
\par If ever I loved Thee, my Jesus, 'tis now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I will love Thee in life; I will love Thee in death,
\par And praise Thee as long as Thou lendest me breath;
\par And say, when the death-dew lies cold on my brow,
\par If ever I loved Thee, my Jesus, 'tis now.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In mansions of glory and endless delight,
\par I'll ever adore Thee and dwell in Thy sight;
\par I'll sing with the glittering crown on my brow,
\par If ever I loved Thee, my Jesus, 'tis now.
\par 
\par  \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
